  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n``_beforeTokenTransfer()`` in ``iTryTokenOFT.sol`` prevents ``blacklisted`` users from transferring any token:\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-brix-money/blob/68bf3dcb7105a1b0ed88b97a57691b0a6230e4e9/src/token/iTRY/crosschain/iTryTokenOFT.sol#L139-L177\n\n``unstake()`` on ``unstakeMessenger.sol`` can be called even by ``blacklisted`` users.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-brix-money/blob/68bf3dcb7105a1b0ed88b97a57691b0a6230e4e9/src/token/wiTRY/crosschain/UnstakeMessenger.sol#L108-L151\n\nThe whole flow works as follows:\n1. Blacklisted user Alice completes cooldown for ``100`` iTRY tokens.\n2. Alice calls ``UnstakeMessenger.unstake(0.05 ETH)``  \n    - Pays 0.1 ETH total (0.05 for spoke→hub, 0.05 for return) │\n    - Message: UnstakeMessage({user: Alice, ...})               │\n    - LayerZero message sent to hub    \n3. LayerZero Endpoint calls ``wiTryVaultComposer._lzReceive()``\n4. ``_lzReceive()`` decodes message and calls ``_handleUnstake()``\n```solidity\nfunction _handleUnstake(..., UnstakeMessage{user: Alice}) {\n    // Check cooldown completed   \n    uint256 assets = StakediTryCrosschain.unstakeThroughComposer(Alice);                                 \n```\n5. StakediTryCrosschain.unstakeThroughComposer(Alice) is called\n6. ``_handleUnstake()`` continues\n```solidity\n        SendParam memory _sendParam = SendParam({\n            dstEid: _origin.srcEid,\n            to: bytes32(uint256(uint160(user))),\n            amountLD: assets,\n            minAmountLD: assets,\n            extraOptions: options,\n            composeMsg: \"\",\n            oftCmd: \"\"\n        });\n\n        _send(ASSET_OFT, _sendParam, address(this));\n```\n7. ``iTryTokenOFTAdapter.send()`` is called\n```solidity\n    - Locks 100 iTRY in adapter\n```\n8. LayerZero Endpoint delivers message \n    - Calls: iTryTokenOFT._lzReceive()\n9. ``iTryTokenOFT._lzReceive()`` executes:\n```solidity\n   address toAddress = Alice\n   uint256 amountReceivedLD = _credit(Alice, 100 iTRY, ...)\n```\n10. ``_credit()`` calls ``_mint()``\n11. ``_mint()`` triggers ``_beforeTokenTransfer()`` which ``reverts()``.\n\nThis is how ``unstake()`` of ``unstakeMessenger.sol`` calls ``_beforeTokenTransfer()`` on ``iTryTokenOFT.sol``.\n\nNow the main problem is when our ``_credit()`` fails due to ``blacklisted``,  our ``100 iTRY`` tokens are still locked in ``iTryTokenOFTAdapter()`` with no ``rescue`` mechanism.\n            \n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSimilar to ``wiTRYOFT.sol``, ``_mint`` the funds to ``owner()`` when blacklisted users transfer:\n```solidity\n./wiTRYOFT.sol\n\n    function _credit(address _to, uint256 _amountLD, uint32 _srcEid)\n        internal\n        virtual\n        override\n        returns (uint256 amountReceivedLD)\n    {\n        // If the recipient is blacklisted, emit an event, redistribute funds, and credit the owner\n        if (blackList[_to]) {\n            emit RedistributeFunds(_to, _amountLD);\n            return super._credit(owner(), _amountLD, _srcEid);\n        } else {\n            return super._credit(_to, _amountLD, _srcEid);\n        }\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "As ``_beforeTokenTransfer()`` and ``blacklisted`` is only checked in ``step 11`` anyone with a valid ``position`` can call ``unstake()`` for ``cross chain claiming``. Here a ``PoC`` to prove that:\n```solidity\n    function test_poc() public {\n        // Setup: Configure hub peer\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        messenger.setPeer(hubEid, hubPeer);\n\n        // Set mock quote\n        uint256 leg1BaseFee = 0.01 ether;\n        mockEndpoint.setQuote(leg1BaseFee, 0);\n\n        // Get exact quote for the return trip value we want to send\n        (uint256 exactFee,) = messenger.quoteUnstakeWithReturnValue(0.00001 ether);\n\n        // Execute unstake with exact quoted fee for any user\n        vm.prank(user);\n        bytes32 guid = messenger.unstake{value: exactFee}(0.00001 ether);\n\n        // Verify guid returned \n        assertTrue(guid != bytes32(0), \"GUID should not be zero\");\n    }\n```\nPaste the above ``PoC`` in ``UnstakeMessenger.t.sol`` and run it using:\n```solidity\nforge test --match-test test_poc -vvv\n```",
